 /*
- * Built-in iOS battery bring-up service. Default: 100%, AC, not charging.
- * negronibattery=1: read-only PM6150 polling every 30 seconds; voltage-derived
- * SOC is an UNCALIBRATED estimate, not a replacement for the Linux QG algo.
- * See report.md for binary evidence, register provenance and integration.
+ * NEGRONI (OnePlus 10 Pro 5G, SM8450): the battery as iOS reads it, an IOPMPowerSource.
+ *
+ * Why (patches/xnu/README-battery.md): the port's earlier class was the sweet
+ * (Redmi Note 10 Pro, PM6150) driver: PM6150 QG/SCHG addresses on SID 0 that do
+ * not exist on SM8450 (SID 0 is PMK8350; 0x1300 is its PON = the keys) and an
+ * arbiter v5 SPMI layer that rejects this v7 arbiter; slop patch 0089 then removed
+ * its personality, so iOS had no power source at all (status bar battery empty).
+ *
+ * On SM8450 the fuel gauge (an external gauge IC, `qcom,external_gauge`) and the
+ * charger are run by the ADSP charger PD and read over GLINK PMIC_RTR_ADSP_APPS;
+ * the HLOS devicetree has no gauge node. Until the ADSP runs (patch 0240 + a
+ * battmgr client), this service measures what the HLOS ADC can reach, through
+ * the PMK8350 VADC (ADC7, SID 0 0x3100; Linux qcom-spmi-adc5.c adc7 path), with
+ * the channels of the live Android DT (vadc@3100):
+ *   0x38f pm8350b_vbat_sns   prescale 1/3      battery voltage (per-cell value, 2S pack)
+ *   0x311 pm8350b_usb_in_v_div_16  1/16        USBIN (VBUS): charger present
+ *   0x3a1 pm8350b_ichg_fb    1000/305185       charge current (uA)
+ *   0x317 pm8350b_iin_fb     32/100            input current (uA)
+ *   0x146 pm8350_hot_pocket_therm  ratiometric skin temperature (OPLUS skin_temp_chan)
+ * State of charge: open-circuit-voltage curve (4.45 V class LiCoO2 cell, the DT's
+ * vfloat 4435 mV, power-off 3300 mV) with charge-current compensation, coulomb
+ * counting of the charge current while charging, monotonic smoothing (never
+ * up on battery, never down on a charger) and a slew limit. It is an ESTIMATE
+ * (NegroniBatterySOCEstimated = true); the discharge current is not measurable
+ * from the HLOS side, so it cannot coulomb-count on battery.
+ *
+ * PMIC writes: only the ADC7 conversion request registers 0x3140-0x3145/0x3147
+ * (as Linux adc7_configure), and only when the arbiter gives that APID to EE 0
+ * (bsd/dev/negroni_spmi.c enforces both). No charger register is touched.
+ *
+ * Boot-arg negronibatt:
+ *   0  no power source (the kernel before this patch)
+ *   1  measured, as above (default)
+ *   2  1 + diagnostics: a raw line per poll and a one-time PM8350B peripheral census
+ *   3  static 100 %, on AC, not charging (the old NegroniBattery fallback; no PMIC access)
+ * Keys follow AppleSmartBattery as the reference ports learned them (bergamota 0130,
+ * HackiOS RedwoodBattery.cpp): CurrentCapacity is the percentage with MaxCapacity 100;
+ * mAh go to AppleRaw*Capacity / NominalChargeCapacity / DesignCapacity.
